# Build context exclusions for backend/Dockerfile (T-DO-1).
#
# Two jobs, and the first one is a security control rather than a size
# optimisation: DO-3 says no environment-specific config is baked into the
# image, and `backend/.env` currently holds a live ANTHROPIC_API_KEY and the
# JWT signing secret. `COPY . .` would put them in a layer that survives every
# later instruction — deleting the file in a subsequent RUN would not remove
# it from the image. Excluding it from the context is what makes that
# impossible rather than merely avoided.

# Secrets and per-developer config. `.env.example` is deliberately NOT
# excluded here — it holds placeholders only — but nothing in the Dockerfile
# copies it either.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# The developer's virtualenv: wrong platform (Windows), and large.
.venv/

# Test and eval code. The pipeline (DO-11) runs the suite on the runner
# against the source tree, not inside this image, so neither belongs in a
# runtime artifact. `evals/` additionally places billed model calls.
tests/
evals/
pytest.ini
.pytest_cache/

# Build/VCS noise.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.git/
.gitignore
.dockerignore
Dockerfile

# Docs and generated artifacts with no runtime consumer. `openapi.json` is
# regenerated from the app and pinned by a test; the served document comes
# from the running app, never from this file.
README.md
CLAUDE.md
openapi.json
